00:30:15.920 --> 00:30:38.390
<v Mira Nair>She was like that, excited and delighted by little things, crossing her fingers before any remotely unpredictable event, like tasting a new flavor of ice cream or dropping a letter in the mailbox. It was a quality he did not understand. It made him feel stupid, as if the world contained hidden wonders he could not anticipate or see.
<v Mira Nair>她就是那样，会被小事所吸引和高兴，在任何稍微不可预测的事情发生之前都会交叉手指，比如品尝一种新口味的冰淇淋或把信扔进邮箱。这是他无法理解的一种品质。这让他觉得自己很愚蠢，仿佛这个世界隐藏着他无法预见或看到的奇迹。

00:30:38.390 --> 00:30:56.450
<v Mira Nair>They had met only four months before. Her parents, who lived in California, and his, who lived in Calcutta, were old friends. And across continents, they had arranged the occasion at which Twinkle and Sanjeev were introduced, a 16th birthday party for a daughter in their circle, when Sanjeev was in Palo Alto on business.
