00:31:44.200 --> 00:32:17.720
<v Mira Nair>She was 27 and recently abandoned, he had gathered, by an American who had tried and failed to be an actor. Sanjeev was lonely, with an excessively generous income for a single man, and had never been in love. At the urging of their matchmakers, they married in India amid hundreds of well wishers whom he barely remembered from his childhood, in incessant August rains, under a red and orange tent strung with Christmas tree lights on Mandeville Road.
<v Mira Nair>她27岁，最近被一个想当演员却失败了的美国人抛弃了。桑杰夫很孤独，作为一个单身汉，他收入优渥，但从未谈过恋爱。在媒人的催促下，他们在印度结婚了，在曼德维尔路，在红橙色的帐篷下，挂满了圣诞灯饰，在不停的八月雨中，身边有成百上千他童年时几乎记不清的祝福者。

00:32:17.720 --> 00:32:46.280
<v Mira Nair>"Did you sweep the attic?" he asked Twinkle later, as she was folding paper napkins and wedging them by their plates. The attic was the only part of the house they had not yet given an initial cleaning. "Not yet. I will, I promise. I hope this tastes good," she said, planting the steaming pot on top of the Jesus trivet. There was a loaf of Italian bread in a little basket, and iceberg lettuce and grated carrots tossed with bottled dressing and croutons, and glasses of red wine. She was not terribly ambitious in the kitchen.
<v Mira Nair>“你打扫阁楼了吗？”桑杰夫后来问特温克尔，当时她正在折叠纸巾并塞在盘子旁边。阁楼是他们房子唯一还没有进行初步清理的地方。“还没有。我会的，我保证。希望这东西味道不错，”她说，把冒着热气的锅放在了那个耶稣隔热垫上面。小篮子里放着一条意大利面包，还有卷心莴苣和磨碎的胡萝卜，拌着瓶装酱汁和面包丁，还有几杯红酒。她在厨房里并不是特别有野心。

